Apache Spark: Apache Spark is open source distributed computing framework for big data processing and machine learning

It follows Master Slave Architecture, one master and all slaves
master: passing orders
Slaves: will be doing work

Driver:
Its Brain of Spark, Creates sparkSession
Converts pyspark code into: Logical plan, Physical Plan and DAG
Sends tasks to executors
colects results

Cluster Manager: The Cluster Manager assigns resources.
Responsible of allocationg resources(CPU & Memory)

Workers:

Machines in the Clusters: 

Each Machine runs Executors

Executors:

Executors on worker nodes run the tasks in parallel.

Each Executor has CPU & Memory

Results are sent back to the Driver.


Task:
Smallest unit of work
one task = One partition processing
Task runs inside the executor

When you write code:

Notebook sends your code(transformations and actions) to driver
Driver creates a logical plan
It optimises the plan using catalyst optimizer
Then logical plan turns to physical plan which is basically set of tasks.
dag scheduler splits into
  Jobs
  stages
  tasks
The driver sends the tasks to executors by cluster
Tasks run in parallel on executors.
Once tasks completed the results are shared to driver.
